            <ArticleTitle>Dramatic lowering of very high Lp(a) in response to niacin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>448-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jacl.2014.03.006</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1933-2874(14)00209-8</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with markedly elevated lipoprotein(a) (Lp(a)) without any other lipid abnormalities. After a myocardial infarction, she was treated with combination of extended-release niacin and statin. An 88% reduction in Lp(a) was observed during 5 years of treatment, which is much better response than usually reported.</AbstractText>
